    <p>
      <strong>Proof of Proposition <a href="/tag/FE4679" data-tag="FE4679">3.1.2.1</a>.</strong>
       Since $p$ is a Cartesian fibration, it induces a map $X^{\natural } \rightarrow S^{\sharp }$ which has the right lifting property with respect to all marked anodyne maps. By Proposition <a href="/tag/B7A488" data-tag="B7A488">3.1.2.3</a>, the induced map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (X^{\natural })^{K^{\flat }} \rightarrow (S^{\sharp })^{K^{\flat }}=(S^ K)^{\sharp } \]
</div>
    <p>
       has the right lifting property with respect to all marked anodyne morphisms. The desired result now follows from Remark <a href="/tag/A433BE" data-tag="A433BE">3.1.1.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
